      "confidence": 0.85,
      "curator_note": "1-Chloro-2-methylpropane (isobutyl chloride) molecular ion, charge and odd electron localized on chlorine (drawn +•). Book draws 1 arc: a straight full (2-electron) arrow above the CH2-Cl bond pointing at Cl. move <1> is drawn and is the complete electron flow (C-Cl bonding pair to Cl); no implicit move is required, giving C4H9+ (m/z 57, 4%) + •Cl. NOTE: the printed base peak here is C3H7+ [100%] (loss of CH2Cl, the far-bond inductive effect the text highlights) and (M-HCl)+• is 7%; these are NOT depicted by this arrow and are not encoded here."
